      [kotlin] fix Semgrep pattern parsing for class/when/enum class bodies
      
      Augment the Kotlin grammar so common Semgrep idioms parse cleanly:
      
      - Single-line `class Foo { ... }` (LANG-476): add a `seq("{", ellipsis,
        "}")` alternative on `class_body` to bypass the `semis`-separator
        requirement on members. This covers `class`, `interface`, `object`,
        generics, annotation classes, and `@A class C { ... }`.
      - `when (x) { ... }` (LANG-480): augment `when_entry` to accept a bare
        ellipsis (with higher precedence than expression-form ellipsis) so
        a `...` is parsed as a stand-alone entry rather than an expression.
      - `enum class E { ... }` (LANG-483): mirror the `class_body` fix on
        `enum_class_body` and extend `enum_entry` to accept `...` for the
        multi-line `enum class E { A, B, ... }` form.
      
      Adds corpus tests covering each affected shape.
      
